  "proof_construction": [
    "One actual half-different B is chosen before all ranks k,m and signatures j.",
    "The same proved real tensor equivalence is followed by conjugation of precisely the original negative tail and a single finite enumeration shared with the coefficient type.",
    "Explicit finite fiber equivalences give p=k+j-1 and q=m-j for the literal original host-root filter.",
    "The coefficient action, complex structure, and normalized integer alternating form remain those of the SAME complete constructed Datum.",
    "The period range equals the integer span of the transported actual integral basis; this proves injectivity, discreteness and full real span.",
    "The source positive Hermitian matrix is constructed, with imaginary part exactly equal to the original EF; no rescaling or period conclusion is assumed."
  ],
  "source_adaptations": [
    "NativeGeometricHost/Datum replace only the namespaces of already reconstructed complete source records.",
    "The general spectral diagonalization is replaced by the explicit already constructed diagonal coordinates; its coefficient-type fiber counts are proved directly.",
    "Only the source pure Hermitian and integral-basis range argument is retained from exists_isPeriod.",
    "Pinned TensorProduct.inductionOn uses tmul/add branches and no obsolete zero branch.",
    "Proof-local Prop classes use anonymous have/let per the pinned warning convention."
  ],
  "sign_convention": "Native field Hermitian form conjugates its FIRST argument; actual positivity is EF(Jx,x)>0. The source period Hermitian form is linear in its FIRST argument and is constructed as B(Ix,y)+i*B(x,y), so Im(hermForm(Px,Py))=EF(x,y) exactly.",
  "period_field_inventory": [
    "actual O(E) coefficient action",
    "injective period map",
    "DiscreteTopology of its range",
    "full real span",
    "positive Hermitian matrix",
    "literal imaginary part equals source-normalized EF"
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "The separate integral symplectic PID basis supplier required by downstream source consumers.",
    "Actual analytic/algebraic uniformization and level/moduli existence (Out.Laws/Laws2, cube and ThetaUnifAV suppliers).",
    "Geometric theta sections, charts and their metric/evaluation attachment.",
    "Separate full Spaces/D7 auxiliary prime T and ray-congruence construction; not needed for this actual period datum."
  ],
